<figure id="S3.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span>Details of our architecture (Projector, Injector, Extractor, Feature Refinement, Segmentation Head). <math id="S3.T2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.T2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> represent the Height and Width of the input image, <math id="S3.T2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[1,4]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[1,4]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.T2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=4</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.T2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\text{classes}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>classes</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\text{classes}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of classes. SAM-L encoder has an embedding dimension of 1024.</figcaption>
